<p>T10 removes profile-email search, display and name fallback from the admin user projections; the signed-in administrator's own Auth email is preserved. T11 rejects email creation/change including super-admin SDK clients, permits historical email removal and unchanged-email unrelated updates, and preserves existing root/role boundaries. These changes remain part of incomplete B03.</p>
<h3 id="new-mandatory-stop">New mandatory stop</h3>
<p>The mandatory actual admin gate failed in <code>web_admin/test/location-relations.emulator.test.ts:34</code>. Its shared station fixture contains private fields and both new-station request calls omit the explicit private state. The new helper correctly fails closed with <code>ContentError: Reload station metadata before continuing.</code> before the stale-location RPC. The test expects <code>functions/failed-precondition</code>, so its intended stale-location assertion is no longer reached. Its concurrent station-creation branch can also accept this early failure without proving the original race behavior.</p>
<p>No source/test fix was made after this mandatory gate failed. Do not weaken the private-revision guard or change the expected rejection to a client error to make the gate pass. The proposed next change is a narrowly scoped test-compatibility amendment: preserve the public-only location fixture or supply explicitly loaded private revision state to both station requests, and retain the actual server stale-location assertion/concurrency coverage. Before touching that currently WO-03-registered test file, I must record the WO-01/R01 write-set and ownership amendment. The existing 33 shared-file owners remain unchanged until an explicit amendment is recorded.</p>
<p>All 17 previously skipped registered cases ran in the actual command:16 passed and the location case failed; the2 new T05 privacy cases passed. This does not waive B15 integration, full Flutter or physical-device obligations, nor close any other finding. Ordinary test19-skips were not counted as passes. Independent B03 review is being collected read-only; B03 is not accepted or complete, and B06 has not started. R01/R10 remain OPEN. No migration, production access, deployment or protected merge was performed.</p>
<p>Continued source/test modifications: <code>web_admin/components/admin/admin-app.tsx</code>, <code>web_admin/components/admin/user-actions-modal.tsx</code>, <code>web_admin/lib/resource-filters.ts</code>, <code>web_admin/test/resource-filters.test.ts</code>, <code>firestore.rules</code>, <code>firebase_tests/firebase-rules/firestore.rules.test.js</code>; execution report and Boss runtime/rendered artifacts also updated.</p>
<h3 id="independent-b03-review-disposition">Independent B03 review disposition</h3>
<p>Independent reviewer <code>wo01_b03_independent_review</code> found no concrete privacy bypass in the current source and independently ran48 focused Node22 cases, all passing with zero skips. The reviewer confirmed the location-test compatibility failure and concealed early rejection in its concurrent branch. <strong>Completion approval is withheld</strong> until the mandatory emulator gate passes on the corrected candidate. The reviewer did not edit files or run emulators/production operations. Browser interaction was not performed; network-error fail-closed handling was source-reviewed but still lacks an explicit SDK failure regression. These remain verification limitations, not passes.</p>
<h2 id="b03-corrected-local-handoff-complete-plan-implementation">B03 corrected local handoff — complete-plan implementation</h2>
<p>The user approved repair-and-rerun within active batches and implementation of all four Work Orders. Baselinec304e85 was clean. I registered the location compatibility test as an additive owned path without changing any original33ownership assignment. The test now strips private fields for its public-only location journey, retains the actual server stale-location assertion, and rejects hidden client-guard failures in its concurrent branch. The isolated offline SDK guard primes cached metadata, disables only its client network, requires a ContentError with no cached/empty state, verifies unchanged persisted projections, and restores network in finally.</p>
<ul><li>Actual admin emulator GREEN:20/20, zero skips (<code>B03-completion-admin-emulator.log</code>), including all17original identities plus3privacy cases.</li><li>Whole admin lint and ordinary tests passed (<code>B03-completion-full-lint.log</code>, <code>B03-completion-full-unit.log</code>). Ordinary skipped emulator cases are not claimed as acceptance; the actual emulator run supplies that evidence.</li><li>Independent reviewerb03_acceptance_review:48/48focused cases passed, no concrete introduced bypass/regression, source/test hashes recorded in reviewer handoff. Local code handoff approved; no finding closure.</li><li>Synthetic browser: logged in to the demo super-admin, station list loaded, editor displayed Canonical synthetic owner from the private document. Actual downloaded workbook has1synthetic row and the canonical private owner, verified through XLSX parsing. The export wait timed out in automation despite successful download; no false product failure or RED is claimed.</li><li>Negative browser role/error checks remain final-QA obligations: Chrome lost debugger attachment after the automation timeout and could not be reattached. Their underlying SDK/Rules permission and offline failure regressions passed. Do not claim the missing browser interactions occurred.</li><li>The first temporary UI fixture exited with an unresolved top-level await before rehearsal; the local runner keep-alive was corrected. This was environment/runner evidence only, not RED. All rehearsal accounts/data/config were synthetic under demo-hudhud-admin-test. Temporary UI server and emulators were stopped afterward; no production access.</li></ul>
<p>B03 is LOCAL_GREEN/INTERIM_HANDOFF for dependent code, with finalbrowserQA explicitly pending. B06 can prepare/test tools; B07 is independently eligible. R01/R10 remain OPEN until all final matrix/operational criteria are proven. FullB15worker integration and physicaldevice/fullFlutter obligations remain unchanged.</p>
<h2 id="b06-verified-demo-only-handoff">B06 verified demo-only handoff</h2>
<p>B06 prepared bounded preview/apply/resume/verification/privacy-safe recovery tooling. The initial37synthetic guards and first10emulator passes did not earn final approval: independent review found unbound claimed transport, expiry before initial lease write, and mutable backup-directory protection. Five permanent review guard assertions reproduced those failures (42tests:37pass/5fail). A further pre-checkpoint directory-drift guard failed (46tests:45pass/1fail). The author corrected the same owned source and retained all failed logs.</p>
<p>Current source uses a factory-owned frozen local demo Firestore transport, rechecks backup/recovery coverage inside initial lease acquisition including empty manifests, and revalidates directory realpath/device/inode/owner/mode for each operation and checkpoint. Revised synthetic46/46 passed independently. Final actual emulator10/10 passed with no skips; B06-final-emulator-provenance.json ties command, input/source/test/Rules/log hashes to that revised candidate. Independent reviewerb06_security_review approved this demo-only code scope. Historical B06-provenance.json is not treated as current acceptance; revised B06-review-provenance.json and final emulator provenance are authoritative.</p>
<p>The first real timestamp assertion compared an unsaved nanosecond value with Firestore's microsecond-precision stored value. It was corrected to establish the persisted preimage/updateTime before migration, then verify exact preservation. The failed guard log is retained as fixture evidence, not vulnerability RED.</p>
<p>Recovery deliberately verifies exact postimages and performs zero data writes: privacy migration changes no safe public field to undo. Moved values remain private and removed profile email remains absent. No claim of whole-snapshot rollback is made. Production mutation is explicitly unavailable; operator backup custody/retention/deletion, supported production execution integration and G-O1-READY/O-1 remain separate unresolved checkpoints. R01/R10 remain OPEN; B15/final QA/device criteria are not waived.</p>
<h2 id="b15-full-nonempty-candidate-rejected-by-independent-review">B15 full nonempty candidate rejected by independent review</h2>
<p>The frozen isolated candidate remains immutable and unintegrated. Independent ordinary Node22 verification executes all 63 existing cases, including the large inventory/union cases: 63/63 pass, zero failures or skips, exit 0. That GREEN result is insufficient for handoff: two separate executed reviewer probes fail their intended rejection assertions with zero skips. One demonstrates late canonical comment version drift proceeding into a created-contribution inverse after recovery/later restore units; the other demonstrates acceptance of a same-body target-head ABA with a changed native version. These are business assertion failures against the actual candidate exports/native model, not missing tests, compilation or environment failures, and not a claim of actual SDK coverage or demonstrated counter loss.</p>
<p>Independent QA also reports closed-purpose-schema/privacy and public clock-override blockers. The new full-tool API must not accept the clock exception approved only for the private QA process boundary. All blockers require permanent regression assertions executed before their fixes, a separate frozen revision, applicable GREEN gates and independent source/security re-review. Existing GREEN tests do not waive them. Review and durable evidence are recorded in B15-nonempty-source-review.md and evidence/WO-04/B15-nonempty-source-review-provenance.json.</p>
<p>The integrated root count tool remains early-bootstrap-only; no full nonempty candidate source was applied. B15 and full 04-T09 remain incomplete, B16 is NOT STARTED, and all R01–R13 findings remain OPEN. Actual SDK recovery/restore/replay, legal mid-flight writer ordering, exact-candidate worker/privacy/Rules integration, the original 17 emulator identities and mandatory full Flutter/browser/physical-device gates remain explicit acceptance obligations. No production operation, migration, deployment, source change, emulator or Flutter run occurred as part of this rejection checkpoint. Historical evidence above is preserved.</p>
